## Summary

Injected `data-semtag-*` hints into **TableSpot** (`WebTestBench_0010`, a restaurant-reservation app) across all four screens/views, per the spec at `references/hint-design.md`.

**Screens & components annotated:**
- **Header** (all pages): logo/nav links (desktop + `.mobile` duplicates per §8), mobile-menu toggle controlling a `region`
- **Home** (`Index.tsx` + `FilterBar.tsx` + `RestaurantCard.tsx`): search input, filter toggle/panel, cuisine & price `select`s (with `data-semtag-options` + individual `option` items), restaurant count/empty observables, and the `restaurants.grid` `collection` with `.item.<id>` cards (nav + rating observable)
- **Restaurant detail** (`RestaurantDetail.tsx` + `ReservationForm.tsx` + `ReviewCard.tsx` + `ReviewForm.tsx`): back link, not-found fallback, name/rating/address/price observables, features `collection`, reviews tabs (`action` + `controls`) with a folded reviews `collection`, full reservation form (date/time/party-size/guest fields/coupon flow/submit), confirmation panel, star-rating picker folded as a `collection` of `action` items, and the write-a-review form
- **My Reservations** (`MyReservations.tsx` + `ReservationCard.tsx`): upcoming/past tabs each `controls`-linked to a folded `collection`, per-tab empty states, and each reservation card (status/coupon observables, modify dialog with time/party-size selects, cancel alert-dialog)
- **404** (`NotFound.tsx`): return-home link

**Id namespaces:** `nav.*`, `search.*` / `filters.*`, `restaurants.grid.*`, `restaurant.detail.*`, `restaurant.reviews.*` / `restaurant.review.*`, `reservation.*`, `reservations.tab.*` / `reservations.upcoming|past.*` / `reservations.list.item.<id>.*`, `notfound.*`.

**Validator:** 79 hinted elements, **0 errors**, 1 expected warning (`select-without-options` on the date picker in `ReservationForm.tsx` — deliberately left without `data-semtag-options` since it opens a 60-day calendar, not an enumerable option list).

**Deliberately left unhinted:**
- Calendar day cells inside the date popover (too granular, no stable enumeration)
- Footer Privacy/Terms/Support spans (inert, no `onClick`, purely decorative)
- Numeric star-rating display on existing reviews (`ReviewCard`) — visually rendered as filled icons with no visible text, so a hint couldn't carry real information without adding visible copy (against the constraints)

**Manual checks performed** (beyond static linting): confirmed every `collection`-role container is a real DOM ancestor of its `.item.` children, and that all template-literal ids (restaurant id, review id, reservation id, feature/cuisine/time/star slugs) stay unique at runtime given the app's data.

**Project checks:** `tsc --noEmit` clean; `npm run build` succeeded; `npm run lint` shows only 3 pre-existing errors/8 warnings, all in files I didn't touch (`ui/command.tsx`, `ui/textarea.tsx`'s empty-interface pattern, `tailwind.config.ts`'s `require()`) — confirmed via `git status`/`diff` that these predate this session.

